        "subject": "LU-19048 tests: use loopback gateways in sanity-lnet",
        "message": "LU-19048 tests: use loopback gateways in sanity-lnet\n\nsanity-lnet test_101, test_103 and test_255 add routes through\ngateways at the local IP address plus 1 to 5. On a shared test\nsubnet, these addresses can be nodes of other test sessions. LNet on\nsuch a node accepts the router ping and adds a peer for this node.\nTests on that node that compare the peer list then fail.\n\nUse gateways in 127.0.0.0/8. The traffic stays on the local node.\nLNet refuses each connection at once, because no local NI has the\ntarget NID.\n\nFixes: 6f1f422d86 (\"LU-16607 tests: Use real IPs for router tests\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet\nTest-Parameters: nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I802e47531fe0b70f5565c559f4de55932f99e1d2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
